{"seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"Related Documentation","anchor":"Related-Documentation","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAPaywall","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginArchitecture"]},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/MacrosReference","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginKillswitchReference","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginParentalGateReference","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginAnalyticsReference","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginFeatureFlagsReference","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStoreGuide","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistenceMiddlewareGuide","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/KeyValueStoreGuide","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoRedo","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/GettingStarted","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Troubleshooting"],"anchor":"Reference","title":"Reference","generated":true}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux"]]},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"sections":[],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"API reference for the "},{"code":"SwiduxPaywall","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" library — paywall presentation, entitlement observation, and purchase orchestration."}],"kind":"article","primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"SwiduxPaywall","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is a domain plugin that owns the paywall slice of your app’s state and routes paywall actions through the Swidux dispatch cycle. It is provider-agnostic: the plugin knows nothing about RevenueCat, StoreKit, products, prices, or purchase results. You supply a "},{"code":"PaywallService","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" conformer that talks to whichever purchase backend you use, and the plugin manages presentation state, async progress, and entitlement transitions."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"For end-to-end wiring, see "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAPaywall","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":". For where this plugin sits in the lifecycle, see "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginArchitecture","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Library-target","level":2,"text":"Library target"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Product: ","type":"text"},{"code":"SwiduxPaywall","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Import: "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"import SwiduxPaywall"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Add the product to your target dependencies in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Package.swift"},{"type":"text","text":" alongside "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Swidux"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Provided-implementations","level":2,"text":"Provided implementations"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The plugin ships with two in-repo conformers, both provider-agnostic and SDK-free:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MockPaywallService"},{"type":"text","text":" — fixed snapshot, stream finishes immediately; for previews and tests."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SimulatedPaywallService"},{"type":"text","text":" — a stateful, fully driveable service. Paired with the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxDevPaywallUI"},{"type":"text","text":" debug sheet, it lets a developer or QA tester grant Pro\/Trial\/Permanent, restore, and simulate failure\/latency — all flowing through the real plugin pipeline, with no SDK and no vendor commitment. Use it as the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"service:"},{"type":"text","text":" while the paywall vendor decision is still open."}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"For production RevenueCat integrations, the ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"https:\/\/github.com\/heirloomlogic\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" companion package provides:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"RevenueCatPaywallService"},{"type":"text","text":" — a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PaywallService"},{"type":"text","text":" conformer that bridges RevenueCat’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"CustomerInfo"},{"type":"text","text":" stream and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"restorePurchases()"},{"type":"text","text":" API."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MockRevenueCatPaywallService"},{"type":"text","text":" — a RevenueCat-flavored mock for previews."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"SwiduxRevenueCatPaywallUI","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" — a SwiftUI sheet built on RevenueCatUI that hands purchase results back through the plugin.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Full API documentation lives in the package’s own "},{"identifier":"https:\/\/heirloomlogic.github.io\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall\/documentation\/swiduxrevenuecatpaywall\/","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"For other backends (StoreKit, custom server), implement "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PaywallService"},{"type":"text","text":" directly — see "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAPaywall","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" Step 3, Path B.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Resilient last-known-good decorator","anchor":"Resilient-last-known-good-decorator","level":3,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"ResilientPaywallService","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" wraps any "},{"code":"PaywallService","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" so a transient failure to read entitlements at cold launch never presents a previously-seen paid user as free. It retries with backoff, then falls back to a last-known-good snapshot persisted through an injected "},{"code":"KeyValueStore","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". Because that cache vouches for a paid entitlement while offline, back it with "},{"code":"KeychainKeyValueStore","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" — not "},{"code":"UserDefaults","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", whose plist a user can edit or restore from a doctored backup:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["let resilient = ResilientPaywallService(","    base: paywallService,","    store: KeychainKeyValueStore(service: \"com.example.myapp\")",")"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Feed the wrapped instance to both "},{"code":"PaywallPlugin(..., service:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and any app-side entitlement reader. The live provider stays authoritative: any successful snapshot overwrites the cache. See the type’s own documentation for the staleness policy and threat model.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Types","anchor":"Types","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"text":"`PaywallPlugin<RootState, RootAction>`","anchor":"PaywallPlugin%3CRootState-RootAction%3E","level":3,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"@MainActor","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"SwiduxPlugin","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" conformer. Owns a slice of root state typed as ","type":"text"},{"code":"PaywallState","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and an action enum typed as ","type":"text"},{"code":"PaywallAction","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["public init(","    state: WritableKeyPath<RootState, PaywallState>,","    action toRootAction: @escaping @Sendable (PaywallAction) -> RootAction,","    extractAction: @escaping @Sendable (RootAction) -> PaywallAction?,","    service: any PaywallService,","    openURL: @escaping @Sendable (URL) async -> Void = { \/* default *\/ }",")"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The default ","type":"text"},{"code":"openURL","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" handler calls ","type":"text"},{"code":"UIApplication.shared.open","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" on UIKit and ","type":"text"},{"code":"NSWorkspace.shared.open","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" on AppKit. Override it for testing or for non-standard environments.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"`PaywallState`","anchor":"PaywallState","level":3,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"Sendable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"Equatable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" struct. The slice the plugin owns.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["public struct PaywallState: Sendable, Equatable {","    public var isPro: Bool","    public var hasPermanentLicense: Bool","    public var isPresented: Bool","    public var requestedReason: String?","    public var isLoading: Bool","    public var error: String?","    public var isCustomerCenterPresented: Bool","    public var isObservingCustomerInfo: Bool","","    public init(","        isPro: Bool = false,","        hasPermanentLicense: Bool = false,","        isPresented: Bool = false,","        requestedReason: String? = nil,","        isLoading: Bool = false,","        error: String? = nil,","        isCustomerCenterPresented: Bool = false,","        isObservingCustomerInfo: Bool = false","    )","","    public var isGateSatisfied: Bool { isPro || hasPermanentLicense }","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"isGateSatisfied","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is the single read your feature code should consult before running gated work. It is ","type":"text"},{"code":"true","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" when the user holds an active pro subscription or a permanent license.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"`PaywallAction`","anchor":"PaywallAction","level":3,"type":"heading"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["public enum PaywallAction: Sendable {","    case request(reason: String)","    case dismiss","    case observeCustomerInfo","    case refreshCustomerInfo","    case customerInfoUpdated(EntitlementSnapshot)","    case refreshFailed(String)","    case restorePurchases","    case presentCustomerCenter","    case dismissCustomerCenter","    case openManageSubscriptions","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"text":"`EntitlementSnapshot`","anchor":"EntitlementSnapshot","level":3,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Provider-agnostic value the service emits to describe the user’s current entitlement.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["public struct EntitlementSnapshot: Sendable, Equatable {","    public let isPro: Bool","    public let hasPermanentLicense: Bool","","    public init(isPro: Bool = false, hasPermanentLicense: Bool = false)","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"text":"`PaywallService` (protocol)","anchor":"PaywallService-protocol","level":3,"type":"heading"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["public protocol PaywallService: Sendable {","    func customerInfo() async throws -> EntitlementSnapshot","    func customerInfoStream() -> AsyncStream<EntitlementSnapshot>","    func restorePurchases() async throws -> EntitlementSnapshot","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"text":"`MockPaywallService`","anchor":"MockPaywallService","level":3,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Test\/preview conformer that returns a fixed snapshot. Its stream finishes immediately."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["public struct MockPaywallService: PaywallService {","    public init(isPro: Bool = false, hasPermanentLicense: Bool = false)","    public func customerInfo() async throws -> EntitlementSnapshot","    public func customerInfoStream() -> AsyncStream<EntitlementSnapshot>","    public func restorePurchases() async throws -> EntitlementSnapshot","}"]},{"level":3,"type":"heading","text":"`SimulatedPaywallService`","anchor":"SimulatedPaywallService"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Stateful "},{"code":"actor","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" conformer for development and QA. Holds the current entitlement and multicasts changes through "},{"code":"customerInfoStream()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", so simulated grants survive a later "},{"code":"refreshCustomerInfo","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"\/","type":"text"},{"code":"restorePurchases","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" exactly as a real service would.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["public actor SimulatedPaywallService: PaywallService {","    public init(","        isPro: Bool = false,","        hasPermanentLicense: Bool = false,","        subsystem: String = \"Swidux\",","        category: String = \"Paywall\"","    )","","    \/\/ PaywallService: customerInfo \/ customerInfoStream \/ restorePurchases","","    \/\/ Simulation surface (not part of PaywallService — driven by the dev UI):","    public func grantPro()","    public func grantTrial()","    public func grantPermanentLicense()","    public func setFree()","    public func setRestoreShouldFail(_ shouldFail: Bool)","    public func setRefreshShouldFail(_ shouldFail: Bool)","    public func setArtificialDelay(_ delay: Duration)","}","","public enum SimulatedPaywallError: Error, Equatable {","    case restoreFailed","    case refreshFailed","}"]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"EntitlementSnapshot"},{"type":"text","text":" only models "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"isPro"},{"type":"text","text":" \/ "},{"code":"hasPermanentLicense","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", so "},{"code":"grantTrial()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" yields "},{"code":"isPro == true","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and is distinguished from "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"grantPro()"},{"type":"text","text":" only in the log line."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"`SwiduxDevPaywallUI`","anchor":"SwiduxDevPaywallUI","level":3,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A separate, opt-in library product ("},{"code":"import SwiduxDevPaywallUI","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":") providing a bare-bones debug paywall sheet. It mirrors the shape of the vendor paywall UI so the call site is unchanged when a real provider is adopted:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["someView.devPaywall(","    state: store.paywall,","    service: simulatedPaywallService,","    onAction: { store.send(.paywall($0)) }",")"]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The sheet shows the live "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PaywallState"},{"type":"text","text":", grant buttons, real Restore\/Refresh flows, and QA failure\/latency toggles. On macOS the sheet uses a 400×600 minimum, matching the vendor paywall UI. Hold a "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"single"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SimulatedPaywallService"},{"type":"text","text":" instance and pass it to both "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Store.configured()"},{"type":"text","text":" (as the plugin’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"service:"},{"type":"text","text":") and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".devPaywall(...)"},{"type":"text","text":":"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","code":["@State private var paywallService = SimulatedPaywallService()","@State private var store: AppStore","","init() {","    let service = SimulatedPaywallService()","    _paywallService = State(initialValue: service)","    _store = State(initialValue: .configured(paywallService: service))","}"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"This is the one place a dev\/QA service is intentionally constructed outside "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Store.configured()"},{"type":"text","text":", because the debug UI must drive the same instance the plugin observes. Swapping to a real provider removes the shared-instance wiring and the "},{"code":"SwiduxDevPaywallUI","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" import along with the two-line "},{"code":"Store.configured()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" change."}]},{"level":2,"text":"Action semantics","anchor":"Action-semantics","type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each case below describes the state mutation the plugin performs and the effect (if any) it returns."}]},{"level":3,"text":"`request(reason: String)`","anchor":"requestreason-String","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Sets "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"isPresented = true"},{"type":"text","text":" and stores "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"requestedReason"},{"type":"text","text":". Returns no effect. Dispatch this when a feature needs to gate behind a purchase."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":3,"text":"`dismiss`","anchor":"dismiss","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Sets "},{"code":"isPresented = false","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and clears ","type":"text"},{"code":"requestedReason","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". Returns an effect that dispatches ","type":"text"},{"code":".refreshCustomerInfo","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" so the entitlement is reconciled after the sheet closes (the user may have purchased while the sheet was up).","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":3,"text":"`observeCustomerInfo`","anchor":"observeCustomerInfo","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Returns a long-lived effect that consumes ","type":"text"},{"code":"PaywallService.customerInfoStream()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and dispatches ","type":"text"},{"code":".customerInfoUpdated","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" for every snapshot. Dispatch once on app launch (typically from a ","type":"text"},{"code":".task","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" on the root view). The effect lives for the duration of the stream. Idempotent: ","type":"text"},{"code":"isObservingCustomerInfo","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" guards against double-subscription, so a re-dispatched ","type":"text"},{"code":".task","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (view identity change, scene reconnect) won’t start a duplicate stream.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":3,"text":"`refreshCustomerInfo`","anchor":"refreshCustomerInfo","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Sets ","type":"text"},{"code":"isLoading = true","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". Returns a one-shot effect that calls ","type":"text"},{"code":"PaywallService.customerInfo()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and dispatches "},{"code":".customerInfoUpdated","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" on success or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".refreshFailed"},{"type":"text","text":" on error."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"customerInfoUpdatedEntitlementSnapshot","level":3,"type":"heading","text":"`customerInfoUpdated(EntitlementSnapshot)`"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Sets "},{"code":"isPro","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"hasPermanentLicense"},{"type":"text","text":" from the snapshot, clears "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"isLoading"},{"type":"text","text":", and clears "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"error"},{"type":"text","text":". Returns no effect. The plugin emits this internally; your code rarely dispatches it directly. Note that the plugin emits this on "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"every"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" snapshot (each "},{"code":"customerInfoStream()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" value, every ","type":"text"},{"code":"refreshCustomerInfo","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"\/","type":"text"},{"code":"restorePurchases","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"), not only on entitlement changes — observe ","type":"text"},{"code":"PaywallState","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (or a value derived from it) for transitions rather than mapping this action directly. See ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginArchitecture#Service-Result-Actions-and-Transition-Observation","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":3,"text":"`refreshFailed(String)`","anchor":"refreshFailedString","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Sets "},{"code":"error","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" to the given message and clears "},{"code":"isLoading","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". Returns no effect."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":3,"text":"`restorePurchases`","anchor":"restorePurchases","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Sets "},{"code":"isLoading = true","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". Returns a one-shot effect that calls "},{"code":"PaywallService.restorePurchases()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and dispatches "},{"code":".customerInfoUpdated","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" on success or "},{"code":".refreshFailed","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" on error."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":3,"text":"`presentCustomerCenter` \/ `dismissCustomerCenter`","anchor":"presentCustomerCenter--dismissCustomerCenter","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Toggle "},{"code":"isCustomerCenterPresented","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". No effects. Bind these to a separate sheet if your purchase backend exposes a customer-center UI (RevenueCat does)."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":3,"text":"`openManageSubscriptions`","anchor":"openManageSubscriptions","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Returns an effect that opens "},{"code":"itms-apps:\/\/apps.apple.com\/account\/subscriptions","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" via the configured "},{"code":"openURL","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" handler. This deep-links into the Settings → Subscriptions page on iOS and the equivalent on macOS."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"text":"Implementing a `PaywallService`","anchor":"Implementing-a-PaywallService","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The plugin is purchase-agnostic. It does not know about products, prices, transactions, or vendor SDKs. Your conformer is responsible for translating whatever a backend reports into an "},{"code":"EntitlementSnapshot","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The protocol has three methods:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"customerInfo() async throws -> EntitlementSnapshot"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" — One-shot fetch of the current entitlement. The plugin calls this from "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".refreshCustomerInfo"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"customerInfoStream() -> AsyncStream<EntitlementSnapshot>"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" — Long-lived stream that yields every time the entitlement changes (purchase completes, subscription expires, family sharing update, etc.). The plugin consumes it from "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".observeCustomerInfo"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"restorePurchases() async throws -> EntitlementSnapshot"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" — Performs a restore against the user’s account and returns the resulting entitlement."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Note what the protocol does "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"not","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" require: no product list, no purchase method, no receipt validation. Purchases happen inside whichever paywall UI you present (a RevenueCat paywall view, your own StoreKit-backed sheet, etc.). The plugin only cares about the entitlement that results."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A typical RevenueCat conformer holds a reference to the SDK and bridges its delegate or async APIs into "},{"code":"EntitlementSnapshot","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" values. A vanilla StoreKit conformer iterates "},{"code":"Transaction.currentEntitlements","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and listens to "},{"code":"Transaction.updates","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". Either way, the plugin stays the same."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginPaywallReference"},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/swidux\/pluginpaywallreference"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Article","role":"article","title":"SwiduxPaywall Reference","modules":[{"name":"Swidux"}]},"references":{"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PluginArchitecture":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginArchitecture","role":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Extend the dispatch cycle with lifecycle hooks — from invisible infrastructure to domain-specific features."}],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/pluginarchitecture","kind":"article","title":"Plugin Architecture"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PluginArchitecture#Service-Result-Actions-and-Transition-Observation":{"abstract":[],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginArchitecture#Service-Result-Actions-and-Transition-Observation","title":"S